+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/dataHolding/13608494> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://rdfs.org/ns/void#Dataset> .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/dataHolding/13608494> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/DiscoveryMetadata> .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/BGSDataHolding/> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#member> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/dataHolding/13608494> .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/ALFRD> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "[Obsolete: use CIGSS] Name introduced by Gillespie et al. (2011) for major intrusions of the Scottish Highlands Ordovician Suite (HIO) that occur in the Alford district and consist of dioritic to granitic rock. They are lithologically associated (diorite, quartz-diorite, tonalite, granodiorite and granite), and lithologically distinct from other intrusions of the Scottish Highlands Ordovician Suite. \r\n\r\nTerm not currently used by BGS."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/CGMGR> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "[Obsolete: use CIGSS] Name introduced by Gillespie et al. (2011) for major and minor intrusions of the Scottish Highlands Silurian Suite (HISL) that display a set of shared characteristics and occur in the north-east part of the Grampian Highlands region, mainly in the vicinity of Deeside. \r\n\r\nTerm not currently used by BGS."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/ESHET> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "[Obsolete: use SHEGR] Name introduced by Gillespie et al. (2011) for major intrusions of the Shetland Islands Suite (SHEGR) that occur east of the Walls Boundary Fault. Intrusions of the Shetland Islands Suite are apparently temporally distinct on either side of the fault. \r\n\r\nTerm not currently used by BGS."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/HIO> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "[Obsolete: use CIGSS] Name introduced by Gillespie et al. (2011) for all components of the Caledonian Supersuite (CIGSS) that occur within the Northern Highlands and Grampian Highlands regions and formed broadly in association with the Grampian Event. This is the older (Ordovician) of the two main tectonothermal events of the Caledonian Orogeny in Scotland. \r\n\r\nTerm not currently used by BGS."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/HISL> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "[Obsolete: use CIGSS] Name introduced by Gillespie et al. (2011) for all components of the Caledonian Supersuite (CIGSS) that occur within the Northern Highlands and Grampian Highlands regions and formed broadly in association with the Scandian Event. This is the younger (Silurian) of the two main tectonothermal events of the Caledonian Orogeny in Scotland. \r\n\r\nTerm not currently used by BGS."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/MSHET> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "[Obsolete: use SHEGR] Name introduced by Gillespie et al. (2011) for minor intrusions of the Shetland Islands Suite (SHEGR) not assigned to other subsuites. \r\n\r\nTerm not currently used by BGS."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/NWGRA> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "[Obsolete: use CIGSS] Term not currently used by BGS."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/WSHET> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasLithologyDescription> "[Obsolete: use SHEGR] Name introduced by Gillespie et al. (2011) for major intrusions of the Shetland Islands Suite (SHEGR) that occur west of the Walls Boundary Fault. Intrusions of the Shetland Islands Suite are apparently temporally distinct on either side of the fault. \r\n\r\nTerm not currently used by BGS."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/HISL> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasYoungestAge> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/DL> .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/HISL> <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/hasYoungestAgeValue> "394.3"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#double> .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/HISL> <http://purl.org/linked-data/registry#status> <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/reg-statuses/deprecated> .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/HISL> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Obsolete name. Igneous intrusive bedrock. Occurs onshore. Emplaced during the Silurian Period - to - Early Devonian Epoch (Devonian Period) (443.1-394.3 Ma BP)."@en .
+<http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit/HISL> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Scottish Highlands Silurian Suite [Obsolete: use CIGSS]"@en .
